;; One mutation per invariant. `:find` must occur EXACTLY ONCE in `:file` —
;; `tools/mutate.cljk` refuses otherwise, because a mutation that landed in a
;; comment or a second call site produces a red suite that proves nothing.
;;
;; ## SCOPE
;;
;; Covers the store and query semantics this namespace actually promises:
;; append-only assertion (duplicates kept, order preserved), retraction of
;; EVERY occurrence, entity-position matching in `get-objects`, the logic-
;; variable convention, join consistency across clauses, `:find` projection,
;; and result deduplication.
;;
;; It does NOT cover `datom.core/eavt` itself — that is another repository's
;; invariant and mutating a dependency from here would measure the wrong
;; suite. It does not cover clause ORDER performance (there is no index; the
;; join is a scan) and it does not cover what happens when `:find` names a
;; variable no clause binds, which is undefined today and has no test.
;;
;; ⚠ These mutations run `kbb -M:test`, the JVM half. This namespace has
;; no reader conditionals in `src/`, so for kgraph the two halves execute the
;; SAME forms and a kill here is a kill there — but that is a property of
;; this file today, not a general one. The cljs half is run by
;; `test/run_portable.cljk` and must be run separately.
;;
;; ## What the suite looked like before, measured
;;
;; Run against the suite as it stood on 2026-08-18 (2 tests, 4 assertions),
;; this table scored 4 killed / 4 SURVIVED. The survivors were
;; `:assert-datom-appends-at-the-end`, `:assert-entities-flattens`,
;; `:results-are-deduplicated` and — the one that matters —
;; `:a-repeated-variable-must-agree-across-clauses`: the join could have been
;; replaced by a cross product and the suite would have stayed green. Ten
;; tests were added with the conversion and the table now scores 8/8. That
;; number is the reason they are there.
;;
;; ## A mutation NOT in this table, and why
;;
;; Renaming a `def`/`defn` (say `query` -> `qry`) was tried and scores
;; UNMEASURED, not killed: the rename breaks the callers, the namespace does
;; not load, and a suite that cannot start has not been shown to notice
;; anything. Mutate a VALUE.
[{:id :assert-datom-appends-at-the-end
  :invariant "the log is append-only and in insertion order"
  :file "src/kotoba/kgraph.cljk"
  :find "  (conj (vec datoms) datom))"
  :replace "  (conj (seq datoms) datom))"}

 {:id :retract-removes-every-occurrence
  :invariant "retract-datom drops all copies, not the ones equal to nothing"
  :file "src/kotoba/kgraph.cljk"
  :find "  (vec (remove #(= % datom) datoms)))"
  :replace "  (vec (remove #(= % ::never) datoms)))"}

 {:id :get-objects-reads-the-entity-position
  :invariant "an [e a v] datom is addressed by e, not by a"
  :file "src/kotoba/kgraph.cljk"
  :find "  (vec (filter #(= e (first %)) datoms)))"
  :replace "  (vec (filter #(= e (second %)) datoms)))"}

 {:id :a-logic-variable-is-spelled-with-a-question-mark
  :invariant "?x binds; a plain symbol is a value to match"
  :file "src/kotoba/kgraph.cljk"
  :find "(str/starts-with? (name x) \"?\")"
  :replace "(str/starts-with? (name x) \"!\")"}

 {:id :a-repeated-variable-must-agree-across-clauses
  :invariant "the join is a join and not a cross product"
  :file "src/kotoba/kgraph.cljk"
  :find "                 (when (= (get bindings pat) val) bindings)"
  :replace "                 bindings"}

 {:id :results-are-deduplicated
  :invariant "distinct rows, per the docstring"
  :file "src/kotoba/kgraph.cljk"
  :find "    (vec (distinct (map (fn [b] (mapv b find)) results)))))"
  :replace "    (vec (map (fn [b] (mapv b find)) results))))"}

 {:id :the-join-starts-from-one-empty-binding-set
  :invariant "seeding with [] answers no to every query, which looks correct"
  :file "src/kotoba/kgraph.cljk"
  :find "                        [{}]"
  :replace "                        []"}

 {:id :assert-entities-flattens
  :invariant "many entities produce one flat datom log"
  :file "src/kotoba/kgraph.cljk"
  :find "  (into (vec datoms) (mapcat dc/eavt entities)))"
  :replace "  (into (vec datoms) (map dc/eavt entities)))"}]
